Subject: [PATCH 06/44] docs: deep-idle research: what stays on in s2idle, ADT
 pre-check, idle A/B

s2idle's wakes add up to about a minute in 38.5 h, so the drain is power
left on: the power-domain counters show all three display pipelines never
powered off in four suspends, held on by the DCP driver's wakeup path. The
ADT, read from m1n1's reserved region, has everything m1n1 needs to boot
the PMP variant. An A/B of the cpuidle states suggests the CPU PD target
residency is far too long. Adds experiment E4 for the external DCPs.

